     "text_1": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "text": "<p>Altera Agilex 5 devices serve a broad range of applications that require high performance, lower power, and smaller form factors. This tier consists of the performance-optimized D-Series FPGAs and the power-optimized E-Series FPGAs. Altera Agilex 5 devices also feature the industry’s first Enhanced DSP with AI Tensor Block, which deliver high-efficiency AI and digital signal processing (DSP) functionality, and the FPGA industry’s first asymmetric applications processor system consisting of dual Arm Cortex-A76 cores and dual Cortex-A55 cores, which enable you to optimize the performance and power efficiency of their workloads. These characteristics make them ideal for midrange FPGA applications across the edge and core including wireless and wireline communications, video and broadcast equipment, industrial applications, test and measurement products, medical electronics, and defense applications.</p>",
      "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/text",
      "textIsRich": "true"
     }
    },
    "container_2": {
     "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
     "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/container",
     "cq:styleIds": [
      "",
      "1717498056876"
     ],
     "container_1": {
      "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
      "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/container",
      "cq:styleIds": [
       "",
       "1717498052331",
       "1717498055877"
      ],
      "table_1": {
       "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
       "text": "<table cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\">\n<tbody><tr><th>E-Series FPGAs and SoCs</th>\n<th>D-Series FPGAs and SoCs</th>\n</tr><tr><td width=\"50%\">E-Series FPGAs and SoCs are optimized for power and size - with 50% lower power while delivering up to 2.5X better performance as compared to Cyclone V devices, also with features including transceiver rates up to 24x28 Gbps, PCIe 4.0x4, 6x25GbE, 3,600 Mbps DDR5, dual core of A55 and dual core of A76 make it ideal for intelligent applications at the edge, embedded, and more.</td>\n<td width=\"50%\">D-Series FPGAs and SoCs are optimized for performance and power efficiency - with 42% lower power while delivering up to 1.5X better performance as compared to Stratix 10 FPGAs, also with features including transceiver rates up to 32x28 Gbps, PCIe 4.0x8, 16x25GbE, 4,000 Mbps DDR5, dual core of A55 and dual core of A76 make it ideal for various applications across multiple markets.</td>\n</tr></tbody></table>",
       "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/table",
       "textIsRich": "true",
       "cq:styleIds": [
        "",
        "",
        "1722939215525"
       ]
      },
      "text_1": {
       "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
       "text": "<p><b>What is the difference between Agilex 5 E-Series and D-Series?</b></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:0\">E-Series is optimized for power and size: 50% lower power and up to 2.5× better performance than Cyclone V, transceivers to 24×28 Gbps, and PCIe 4.0 x4. D-Series is optimized for performance: 42% lower power and up to 1.5× better performance than Stratix 10, transceivers to 32×28 Gbps, and PCIe 4.0 x8.</p>\n<p><b>What is the AI Tensor Block in Agilex 5?</b></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:0\">Agilex 5 includes an Enhanced DSP with AI Tensor Block for high-efficiency AI and DSP. Peak INT8 throughput reaches 25.99 TOPS on the E-Series A5E 065A and 56.22 TOPS on the D-Series A5D 064, with variable-precision DSP blocks.</p>\n<p><b>What processors are in the Agilex 5 hard processor system?</b></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:0\">The SoC uses an asymmetric applications processor: dual Arm Cortex-A76 cores up to 1.8 GHz and dual Cortex-A55 cores up to 1.5 GHz, with up to 2 MB shared L3 cache. That pairing balances performance and power by workload.</p>\n<p><b>Which memory and interface standards does Agilex 5 support?</b></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:0\">DDR5 to 4,000 Mbps on D-Series and 3,600 Mbps on E-Series, plus DDR4, LPDDR4, and LPDDR5. Connectivity includes PCIe 4.0, up to 6×25GbE on E-Series and 16×25GbE on D-Series, MIPI D-PHY, LVDS at 1.6 Gbps, and TSN.</p>\n<p><b>What applications is the Agilex 5 mid-range FPGA aimed at?</b></p>\n<p style=\"margin-top:0\">Midrange edge and core designs: wireless and wireline communications, video and broadcast, industrial, test and measurement, medical electronics, and defense. Named focus markets are image sensor processing, autonomous mobile robots, and clinical systems, including battery-powered clinical equipment.</p>",
       "sling:resourceType": "macnicaglobal2/components/content/text",
       "textIsRich": "true"
      }
     },
